2.4.2. Risky-response time
The risky-response time is divided into two parts: risk perception time and risk decision-making time. Risk perception time refers to the time difference between the appearance of the risk and participants detecting the risk. And risk decision-making time refers to the time when participants provide feedback after detecting the risk, as shown in Fig. 4 .

